    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the owner's date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), touching two files:\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (source of the generated `OwnerDto`)\n- Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) to the `Owner` schema.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions to reflect the fiscal-year semantics.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Added a `fiscalYear(owner)` mapping to `OwnerDto` and a `fiscalYear(Owner)` helper returning `FY<YY>`.\n- Added a private `fiscalYearValue(LocalDate)` helper: the fiscal year starts 1 July and is labelled by the calendar year it ends in, so a date on/after 1 July rolls into the next year (e.g. `2026-08-11 \u2192 FY27`, `2026-01-05 \u2192 FY26`).\n- Changed `membershipNumber` so its `-M<YY>` segment now uses the fiscal-year YY (matching `fiscalYear`), instead of the calendar year.\n- Changed the tenure component of `membershipPoints` to count **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYearValue(now) - fiscalYearValue(registrationDate) > 1`) rather than a 365-day window. A newly created owner still has zero tenure, so it never earns those points \u2014 preserving existing point/level behaviour.\n\nThe audit log confirms the new behaviour: for a registration date of `2026-08-11`, membership numbers now end in `-M27` (fiscal year FY27), consistent across the endpoint response and the audit line.\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: no test pins the exact fiscal-year label, so I chose the **Australian convention** (label by the ending calendar year \u2014 the 1 Jul 2026\u201330 Jun 2027 year is `FY27`), which matches the codebase's clearly Australian context (NSW/VIC/QLD regions, `Australia/*` timezones, `+61` phone codes). It's documented in both the OpenAPI schema and the mapper Javadoc.",
